/*
 * Every primitive of the SFL runtime, in one place.
 *
 * The C runtime includes this to declare and to tabulate them; the sbt build reads
 * it to generate the Scala table the compiler consults when deciding what a call
 * lowers to. Keeping one list means the two can never disagree about a name, an
 * arity or a signature.
 *
 *   SFL_PRIM(name, symbol, signature, min_arity, max_arity, module)
 *
 * max_arity -1 means variadic. `module` is the .c file that defines it, which is
 * also the granularity at which the linker drops what a program does not use.
 */


